//? Title: Continuous Gain-Ratio Trees: A Checked C4.5-Inspired Learner
//? Subtitle: Actual threshold candidates, iris cross-validation and the original three Gaussian clouds
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A continuous decision tree asks binary threshold questions until it reaches a
class label. We derive information gain and gain ratio on four hand-checkable
rows, inspect the candidates actually considered by datamunge, and evaluate
five-fold predictions on the native iris dataset. The original 180-point,
three-cloud experiment remains as a training-fit control. The existing c45_train
API implements a restricted, unpruned, maximum-ratio learner inspired by C4.5;
it omits C4.5's average-gain filter, categorical and missing-value machinery,
pruning and later threshold penalties. New native tracing exposes actual row
memberships, candidate scores and stopping reasons, without replaying training.
)

\toc

> Four rows: derive the first split

Use two identical numeric features with rows (0,0), (1,1), (2,2), (3,3),
and labels 0,0,1,1. Parent class entropy is one bit. For class proportions p_c,
with zero terms omitted, define

\[
H(S)=-\sum_c p_c\log_2 p_c,\qquad
G(S,t)=H(S)-p_LH(L)-p_RH(R),
\]
\[
I(S,t)=-p_L\log_2p_L-p_R\log_2p_R,\qquad R(S,t)=G(S,t)/I(S,t).
\]

At t=1.5 each child is pure, so G=I=R=1. At t=0.5 the left child
has one class-zero row and the right has labels 0,1,1: conditional entropy
is three quarters times H(1/3,2/3), giving G about 0.311278 and ratio about
0.383689. Every boundary splits nonempty groups, so I is positive. Both
features offer identical candidates; the first strict maximum chooses feature
zero. The diagram uses the actual model and trace memberships.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/c45_threshold.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::c45_train_trace({{0,0},{1,1},{2,2},{3,3}},{0,0,1,1},{1,2,0});
  const auto& root=trace.tree.nodes[0];
  if(root.feature!=0 || root.threshold!=1.5 || trace.candidates.size()!=6) return 1;
  std::print("| feature | threshold | left rows | right rows | conditional entropy | gain | split information | ratio | selected |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto& c:trace.candidates)
    std::print("| {} | {:.1f} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {} |\n",
        c.feature,c.threshold,c.left_count,c.right_count,c.conditional_entropy,c.gain,c.split_info,c.ratio,c.selected);
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(70,1000);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.width=4.4;node.height=1.8;
  diagram.node("root",{0,0},std::format("feature {} <= {}\nrows {}\nH = {} bit",root.feature,root.threshold,
      trace.nodes[0].rows,trace.nodes[0].entropy),node);
  node.fill={220,252,231};node.width=4.2;
  for(auto [id,x,name]:std::vector<std::tuple<int,double,std::string>>{{root.left,-3.5,"left"},{root.right,3.5,"right"}}) {
    const auto& child=trace.tree.nodes[id];
    diagram.node(name,{x,-3},std::format("predict class {}\nrows {}\nH = {} bits",child.prediction,trace.nodes[id].rows,
        trace.nodes[id].entropy),node).edge("root",name,name=="left"?"true":"false");
  }
  diagram.text({0,-4.6},"gain = 1 bit; split information = 1 bit; gain ratio = 1",18)
      .save_svg("build/c45_threshold.svg");
  std::print("\nActual candidates: {}; candidate row tests: {}; owned model nodes: {}.\n",
      trace.candidate_count,trace.candidate_row_tests,trace.tree.nodes.size());
}
```
