| depth cap | full-data nodes | training correct / 150 | five-fold correct / 150 | training fraction | cross-validation fraction |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1 | 3 | 100 | 100 | 0.666667 | 0.666667 |
| 2 | 5 | 144 | 137 | 0.960000 | 0.913333 |
| 3 | 9 | 146 | 138 | 0.973333 | 0.920000 |
| 4 | 13 | 147 | 140 | 0.980000 | 0.933333 |
| 5 | 17 | 150 | 141 | 1.000000 | 0.940000 |
| 6 | 17 | 150 | 141 | 1.000000 | 0.940000 |

Full-data root: Petal.Length <= 2.450; gain 0.918296, ratio 1.000000; sizes 50 and 100.
Root candidates: 119; actual candidate row tests: 17850.
\image(figures/c45_iris.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Full-data training fit and five-fold held-out predictions at each depth cap. The held-out curve need not improve as the tree grows.)
\alttext(Two curves compare correct training and cross-validation fractions across depth limits one through six, with the numerical values printed in the table.)

The depth cap is a growth control, not statistical pruning. With a fixed root
and deterministic search, relaxing it only refines leaves. Child majorities
cannot have fewer total correct training labels than retaining the parent's
majority at those rows. Thus training fit cannot decrease solely from deeper
growth; this argument places no lower bound on held-out accuracy.

> Retain the original three-cloud experiment

The original report generated sixty points per centre at (0,0), (6,0) and
(3,6), coordinate standard deviation 0.6, with mt19937_64 seed five. That
reusable generator now lives in dm::datasets::gaussian_blobs(). It preserves
centre/row/coordinate draw order and has no shared RNG state. The C++ normal
distribution can differ across standard libraries, so the seed is a same-toolchain
repeatability guarantee, not a promise of portable bit-identical coordinates.
The current program prints the actual full tree as flat nodes, then recreates
the original training-accuracy-versus-depth plot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/c45_accuracy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto data=dm::datasets::gaussian_blobs({{0,0},{6,0},{3,6}},60,.6,5);
  std::vector<double> depths,accuracy;
  std::print("| depth cap | nodes | training correct / 180 | training fraction |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t depth=1;depth<=6;++depth) {
    const auto model=dm::algorithms::c45_train(data.features,data.labels,depth,2);std::size_t correct=0;
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<data.labels.size();++i) correct+=dm::algorithms::c45_predict(model,data.features[i])==data.labels[i];
    depths.push_back(depth);accuracy.push_back(static_cast<double>(correct)/data.labels.size());
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} |\n",depth,model.nodes.size(),correct,accuracy.back());
  }
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::c45_train_trace(data.features,data.labels);
  if(data.features.size()!=180 || trace.tree.nodes.size()!=5 || accuracy.back()!=1) return 1;
  std::print("\n| node | depth | row count | majority / leaf label | kind | feature | threshold | left | right |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t id=0;id<trace.tree.nodes.size();++id) {
    const auto& node=trace.tree.nodes[id];
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {} | {} |\n",id,trace.nodes[id].depth,trace.nodes[id].rows.size(),
        node.prediction,node.leaf?"leaf":"split",node.feature,node.threshold,node.left,node.right);
  }
  std::print("\nActual whole-tree candidates: {}; candidate row tests: {}.\n",trace.candidate_count,trace.candidate_row_tests);
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create().line(depths,accuracy,"training fit",{37,99,235},2.5)
      .points(depths,accuracy,"",{37,99,235},4).abline_h(1,{22,163,74},1)
      .title("Original three Gaussian clouds: training accuracy")
      .x_label("maximum split depth").y_label("training correct fraction").y_limits(.5,1.08)
      .save_svg("build/c45_accuracy.svg");
}
```
